/T (Understanding where your data lives is the first step toward writing high-performance Go. The Stack is about locality and speed, while the Heap is about longevity and flexibility.)
/E (Understanding where your data lives is the first step toward writing high-performance Go. The Stack is about locality and speed, while the Heap is about longevity and flexibility.)
