/P 384 0 R
/T (The "Stack" Advantage: Because stack memory is linear, the CPU can predict the next memory address easily. This keeps the Instruction Pipeline full and your code running at max speed.)
/E (The "Stack" Advantage: Because stack memory is linear, the CPU can predict the next memory address easily. This keeps the Instruction Pipeline full and your code running at max speed.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
