188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 385 0 R
/T (The "Heap" Tax: Every time a variable "Escapes" to the heap, you aren't just paying for the memory; you are adding a tiny bit of latency to every future GC cycle. In a microservice processing 10k requests per second, these "tiny bits" add up to significant p99 spikes.)
